A||N||6||Monkeyman||Clutch/Cruise Control switch questions||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||09-06-2001||07:39 PM||||Which of the two switches by the clutch is for the cruise control?  How can I adjust it?  I have to hold the pedal up with my foot to keep the cruise on.  (Almost stays by itself.  A 1/4" adjustment would take care of things.)  Somehow I just can't picture doing that all the way to Chicago.  Is there some way to bypass the switch?<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||09-06-2001||08:07 PM||||You don't want to by-pass the switch because if you press the clutch in the cruise won't shut off and the engine will race up to try and maintain speed. The switch is located on the left side of the clutch pedal. Just loosen the mounting screws and adjust it. I don't remember if its on or off the switch to work. You can go under and look. Just lift up the pedal and see which switch is affected by it. Then adjust that switch in the direction you need to go. <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Archie||09-06-2001||08:07 PM||||One of them is brake light and the other is cruise. The brake is the one that is on the right. It's easy to adjust..... just grab ahold of both switches and push them away from you toward the floor as far as you can...... they will self adjust the first time you push the brake pedal down.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000003||Archie||09-06-2001||08:14 PM||||OOOops sorry, I thought you said brake pedal.<P>nevermind||||reg||1
Z||000004||SLYGUY||09-07-2001||04:37 AM||||I just got my 88GT and the cruise doesn't work. Is this gonna be a vacuum thing? I looked for a blow fuse but there isn't one just for that alone. Will this switch on the clutch pedal fix that? Where should I start?<P>Sly||||reg||5
Z||000005||Monkeyman||09-07-2001||05:24 AM||||Good point, Oreif.  I'll just try to adjust it. Thanx.<P>Don't worry about getting confused, Archie.  You just let me drive your drag car this weekend and you'll feel much better.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||09-07-2001||07:57 PM||||The starter interlock should have heavier wires on it than the cruise switch.<P>Sly,<P>There's a number of things it could be. You will have to check them one at a time untill you find it. Unfortunatly for you only the 87-88 4 cylinder cars have cruise integrated into the ECM. On those cars you can use an ECM scanner to check all the controls.<P>I'd start with vacuum plumbing and the prone to rust vacuum reserve can.||||reg||1
